{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on 48013952 (R16: Lending compatibility and reserved descendants). This narrows d31ea3d2, item 1.\n\n1. Lending compatibility. No signed release exists for the hosted Lending room. It was set up by direct activation on 14 October, and no installation tuple was recorded. So use a finite legacy tuple that exists:\n   - the dap-lending room only: register 5, directory 5, membership 4, rules 3, destination 2, inbox 1, as read back in 99d86feb;\n   - its exact scope references and the definition pins recorded in its Rules;\n   - one grant, for the shelf/ prefix only.\n   The planner reads the exact references and pins from the live room and puts them in an owner-only file before the R16 head goes to review. Build the tuple shape now; do not invent a release binding. dap-lending-demo-1014 gets no entry. The entry ends when Lending moves to a signed release that declares shelf/ itself.\n\n2. Reserved descendants. Your interpretation is confirmed:\n   - a prefix never grants reserved descendants;\n   - the fixed reserved leaf names stay denied at every publication;\n   - install refuses a prefix that is rooted in a fixed reserved path or that overlaps an added authority or rules pattern;\n   - an overlap that cannot be proved absent fails closed.\n   So shelf/ installs under the baseline rules, shelf/AGENTS.md never publishes, .github/ never installs, and shelf/ does not install where an added pattern protects shelf/**. Recheck current evidence at each write, as you propose.\n\n3. Order is unchanged. The archive items keep priority.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}